WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.380
We may never know what's
nudging Oort Cloud

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:05.150
objects out of orbit.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.760
But it's not the only
mystery out there.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:12.500
We still don't know
where the solar system

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.100
ends.

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:16.130
Finding the edge of the
solar system helps us

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:17.990
with the bigger problem
of understanding the

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:19.190
solar system as a whole.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:21.050
How do you know when you
have the whole solar

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:22.820
system until you found
the edge?

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.200
Maybe the biggest mystery
of all is that our sun

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.010
has too much stuff.

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.610
It's wandering the
cosmos with more than its

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.940
fair share. It's
possible our sun is a

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:38.450
thief that robbed its
sisters and brothers in a

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:39.680
cosmic womb.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:43.400
But that extra stuff
could be our ticket out

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.610
when the sun turns up
the heat on us.

